Fix build against modern GLib (this overlay currently has glib-2.90.0
installed): glibmm 2.66 predates GLib's G_DECLARE_FINAL_TYPE() macro being
used for GDBusActionGroup and GEmblem. That macro expands the *Class
typedef as an anonymous struct literal typedef'd directly to the class
name (not a named "struct _FooClass" tag), so glibmm's own generated
forward declaration for the Class type ("using FooClass = struct
_FooClass;") collides with GLib's declaration once both are visible in
the same translation unit:

  error: typedef redefinition with different types
  ('struct _GDBusActionGroupClass' vs 'struct GDBusActionGroupClass')

Since GLib's typedef is an anonymous-struct typedef, glibmm cannot
provide its own compatible forward declaration for it at all (that's only
possible for named/tagged struct types) -- the only fix is to stop
declaring it ourselves and instead make sure GLib's own header, which
already provides a valid FooClass typedef, is visible before glibmm's
header needs the name. The type is only usable from inside <gio/gio.h>
(GLib's public gdbusactiongroup.h/gemblem.h refuse direct inclusion), so
pull that in explicitly rather than relying on include order from
whatever consumer happens to include giomm/{dbusactiongroup,emblem}.h.

giomm/private/{dbusactiongroup,emblem}_p.h reference the type by name
only (BaseClassType = GFooClass), so they still resolve fine once GLib's
declaration is visible.

This overlay disables maintainer-mode for this ebuild (see the ebuild
itself), so it's the pre-generated untracked/ files that need patching,
not the gmmproc .hg templates / tools/m4 macros that would normally
generate them.

--- a/untracked/gio/giomm/dbusactiongroup.h
+++ b/untracked/gio/giomm/dbusactiongroup.h
@@ -25,11 +25,11 @@
 #include <glibmm/object.h>
 #include <giomm/actiongroup.h>
 #include <giomm/remoteactiongroup.h>
+#include <gio/gio.h>


 #ifndef DOXYGEN_SHOULD_SKIP_THIS
 using GDBusActionGroup = struct _GDBusActionGroup;
-using GDBusActionGroupClass = struct _GDBusActionGroupClass;
 #endif /* DOXYGEN_SHOULD_SKIP_THIS */


--- a/untracked/gio/giomm/emblem.h
+++ b/untracked/gio/giomm/emblem.h
@@ -24,11 +24,11 @@

 #include <glibmm/object.h>
 #include <giomm/icon.h>
+#include <gio/gio.h>


 #ifndef DOXYGEN_SHOULD_SKIP_THIS
 using GEmblem = struct _GEmblem;
-using GEmblemClass = struct _GEmblemClass;
 #endif /* DOXYGEN_SHOULD_SKIP_THIS */
